spec ri06-parallel-edges-disjoint-lpg: 2 sessions, 6 permutations
# RI06, parallel edges. s1 SETs r.w on edge id 1, s2 on edge id 2; both run from a
# to b. The catalogue expects no conflict: the two are different relationships.
# Through the lpg API: SetEdgePropertyByHandle on each instance.
# The final dangling probe must count 0 in every permutation: an edge to a dead node
# is never committed (catalogue §9 point 3).

starting permutation: s1w s1c s2w s2c
step s1w: lpg: SetEdgePropertyByHandle(a, b, <id 1>, w, 1)
step s1c: lpg: Session.EndVersionedTx
step s2w: lpg: SetEdgePropertyByHandle(a, b, <id 2>, w, 2)
step s2c: lpg: Session.EndVersionedTx
final weights: MATCH (:N {name:'a'})-[r]->(:N {name:'b'}) RETURN r.id AS id, r.w AS w ORDER BY id
id|w
--+-
1 |1
2 |2
(2 rows)
final final: MATCH (n) RETURN n.name AS name ORDER BY name
name
----
"a" 
"b" 
(2 rows)
final edges: MATCH (x)-[r]->(y) RETURN x.name AS src, r.id AS id, y.name AS dst ORDER BY src, id, dst
src|id|dst
---+--+---
"a"|1 |"b"
"a"|2 |"b"
(2 rows)
final dangling: <lpg: arcs touching a dead node, at a fresh snapshot>
live_arcs|dangling
---------+--------
2        |0       
(1 row)

